<title>USA: Atlantic to buy 30 planes from Bombardier.</title>
<headline>Atlantic to buy 30 planes from Bombardier.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>ASA Holdings Inc unit Atlantic Southeast Airlines Inc said Monday that it has executed a purchase agreement with Bombardier Inc to acquire 30 Canadair Regional Jet aircraft with options for an additional 60 aircraft.  This transaction includes a definitive financing commitment from the Export Development Corp of Canada.</p>
<p>The company did not disclose the cost of the purchase.</p>
<p>Atlantic Southeast is an Atlanta-based regional air carrier, and offers service to 22 cities form a second hub in Dallas, Texas.</p>
